---
/**
 * How BotMatch works — the page the commission claim rests on.
 *
 * FOUR PARAGRAPHS OF PURE TEXT, and the one thing it is asking a stranger to
 * believe is an ORDER OF OPERATIONS: suitability decides the product, and money
 * is only allowed to break a tie between offers afterwards. An order is a
 * sequence, and a sequence is a drawing. The figure sits under the standfirst
 * rather than at the end, because a reader who does not accept the claim will
 * not read to the end to find it.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BotMatchExplainer from "../components/diagrams/BotMatchExplainer.astro";
---
<Base title="How BotMatch works" description="How BotMatch chooses a robot for you: the questions it asks, the exclusions it applies first, and why it is willing to tell you to buy the cheap one.">
  <h1>How BotMatch works</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="font-size:18px; max-width:680px;">BotMatch is a deterministic, auditable engine — the same answers always produce the same recommendation, and commission can never influence which product it picks.</p>

  <BotMatchExplainer />

  <h2>1. You answer a few questions</h2>
  {/* WAS "Pool type, your main problem…" — the pool questionnaire's own list,
      written when pool was the only category with questions. This page now
      describes a finder that covers nine categories, and naming one category's
      questions as though they were everyone's is the same mistake /botmatch/
      itself used to make. */}
  <p>What the robot is for, where it has to work, what you want it to handle, and your budget. The questions differ by category — a lawn is not a pool — and nothing personal is required.</p>

  <h2>2. We score products on suitability only</h2>
  <p>Each product is scored on how well it fits your answers — cleaning coverage, power match, budget fit and pool-size capability. Products that can't work for you (wrong environment, too small for your pool, or the wrong <em>class</em> — a surface skimmer when you need a full clean) are excluded outright.</p>

  <h2>3. Then — and only then — we pick the best offer</h2>
  <p>After the product is chosen, we rank retailer offers by total price, delivery speed, warranty and how fresh the price data is. Commission is used only as a tie-break between offers that are otherwise equivalent — never to change the product.</p>

  <h2>4. Everything is recorded</h2>
  <p>Every recommendation stores your answers, the exact engine version, and the score of every candidate — so we can prove the recommendation was about fit, not money.</p>

  {/* Points at the universal finder, not at the pool funnel. A reader who
      arrived here from the lawn hub was previously handed a swimming pool. */}
  <p style="margin-top:26px;"><a class="btn primary" href="/botmatch/">Try BotMatch</a></p>
</Base>
